# DFS vs BFS

## Core Difference

### DFS (Depth First Search)

- Go as deep as possible before backtracking.
- Uses Recursion or Stack.
- Good for exploring connected components.

```text
A
|
B
|
C
|
D
```

Traversal:

```text
A → B → C → D
```

---

### BFS (Breadth First Search)

- Explore level by level.
- Uses Queue.
- Good for shortest distance/time problems.

```text
      A
     / \
    B   C
   / \
  D   E
```

Traversal:

```text
A
B C
D E
```

---

# When to Use DFS

Use DFS when the goal is to:

- Explore a connected component
- Count islands
- Calculate area
- Flood Fill
- Check path existence
- Backtracking

### Keywords

```text
Connected
Island
Region
Cluster
Flood Fill
Area
Explore
```

### Examples

- 200. Number of Islands
- 695. Max Area of Island
- 733. Flood Fill
- 79. Word Search
- 130. Surrounded Regions

